# 3-LED Sequential Blinking (Traffic Light Pattern)

## Description
A simple Arduino project that blinks three LEDs (red, yellow, green) in sequence, 
simulating a basic traffic light pattern. Each LED turns on and off with a 500ms 
delay before moving to the next one in the cycle.

## Components Used
- Arduino Uno R3
- 3x LEDs (Red, Yellow, Green)
- 3x Resistors (current-limiting)

## Circuit Connections
| Component | Arduino Pin |
|-----------|-------------|
| Red LED | Digital Pin 13 |
| Yellow LED | Digital Pin 12 |
| Green LED | Digital Pin 11 |

## How It Works
1. Red LED turns ON for 500ms, then OFF.
2. Yellow LED turns ON for 500ms, then OFF.
3. Green LED turns ON for 500ms, then OFF.
4. The cycle repeats continuously.
5. Serial Monitor logs each LED's ON/OFF state for tracking.

